  },
  "color": {
   "note": "photo - dark charcoal chassis, silver MICs, dark blue RE panel and fan door (Juniper's MX80-era styling)"
  },
  "front": {
   "note": "photo - MIC row y 7-41.5 with slots at x 25.0 and 193.4 (the reference unit carries the 20x1GE SFP MIC and the 2x10GE XFP MIC); PS 0/PS 1 at x 14.7/86.2 in the lower band; the blue RE panel from 162.6 to 406 carrying CONSOLE over AUX (x 190), ETHERNET over USB (x 213), EXT CLK A over B (x 232), the SYS OK / RE lamps and ONLINE/OFFLINE button at its left, and the four fixed XFP cages at centres 261.6-349.7 with LINK lamps, silkscreened 0-3 over 0/MIC 0; the MX80 badge at 355; the fan-tray door at 407-445"
  },
  "lifecycle": {
   "note": "announced - the whole MX5-MX80 family is EOL (guide banners and family tables); per-SKU dates on the Juniper milestones page"
  },
  "other-faces": {
   "note": "near-blank by evidence - rail bands estimated; axis conventions per viewer3d.js as the siblings"
  },
  "power": {
   "note": "NOT STATED at chassis level in the extraction; per-module rows were not captured either. The L27/L29 warnings stand as the record"
  },
  "rear": {
